# Question 01 :
What are semantic HTML elements? Why is using them important for web
development?

# Answer 01:
Semantic HTML elements are HTML tags that clearly describe the meaning and purpose of the content they contain. These elements help both the browser and developers understand the structure of a webpage.

Examples of semantic HTML elements include:

<header>, <nav>, <section>, <article>, <footer>, and <main>.
For example:

<header> – Defines the header section of a webpage.

<nav> – Contains navigation links.

<section> – Represents a section of content.

<article> – Represents independent content like a blog post.

<footer> – Defines the footer of the page.

