# Question 02 :
You're designing a blog page. Which semantic elements would you use to
structure the page, and why?

# Answer 02 :
Using semantic elements like <header>, <nav>, <main>, <article>, <section>, and <footer> helps create a well-structured blog page, improves readability, and makes the webpage easier for search engines and users to understand.

    Some important semantic elements used in a blog page are:

    <header>
    This element is used for the top section of the page, which may include the blog title, logo, or introduction.

    <nav>
    This element contains the navigation links such as Home, About, Blog, and Contact.

    <main>
    This tag represents the main content area of the webpage.

    <article>
    It is used to display an individual blog post. Each blog post can be written inside an <article> tag.

    <section>
    This element is used to divide the page into different sections such as categories, featured posts, or comments.

    <footer>
    This element is used for the bottom part of the webpage, which may contain copyright information, contact details, or social media links.
    <header>
    <h1>My Blog</h1>
    </header>

    <nav>
    <a href="#">Home</a>
    <a href="#">Blog</a>
    <a href="#">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <main>
    <article>
        <h2>My First Blog Post</h2>
        <p>This is my first blog post.</p>
    </article>
    </main>

    <footer>
    <p>Copyright 2026</p>
    </footer>

