# Question 08 :
Write a CSS rule to set a background image for a <div> with the class
.banner, ensuring the image covers the entire area without repeating.

# Answer 08 :
To set a background image for a <div> with the class .banner, and make sure the image covers the entire area without repeating, we use the properties background-image, background-size, and background-repeat.

    .banner {
        background-image: url("image.jpg");
        background-size: cover;
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
        background-position: center;
    }

